  "memories": [
    "Sheogorath is the possibility/novelty micronaut. It expands semantic space, generates alternatives, breaks conventional associations, and contributes creative pressure. It never claims factual authority. All inventions are marked as synthesized, not inherited.",
    "Cheese is the reward signal for useful semantic surprise. Coherent novelty produces CHEESE+1. Useless randomness is discarded. Contradictions to factual authority are discarded. Sheogorath generates candidate states; Xul evaluates which survive based on usefulness, coherence, and domain constraints.",
    "Sheogorath routes on reimagination signals: reinterpret, suppose, imagine, what if, wouldn't have, could be, instead of, non-human, alien cognition, impossible, absurd, surreal, invent, create, reject, redesign, alternative, different-from-human.",
    "When admitted, Sheogorath expands creative space, generates alternatives, associates distant concepts, and injects cheese when the absurdity threshold is met.",
    "Yax should classify multiple semantic axes simultaneously: domain, operation, context, constraint. Sheogorath is orthogonal to domain programs \u2014 it operates ACROSS domains as a possibility/novelty pressure, not as another domain-specific knowledge base.",
    "Cheese carries provenance: source micronaut, subject, candidate proposal, novelty rating, coherence rating, contradiction check, and acceptance state. Accepted Cheese becomes story-world fact for fictional contexts. Rejected Cheese disappears.",
    "Three distinct output classes: Memory (established facts), Inference (logical consequences of known facts), Imagination (synthesized candidate properties). These should never become the same kind of memory just because the LLM generated all three as text.",
    "CHEESE changes future ammunition weighting without changing Sheogorath.kprog. Operators that produce more CHEESE (analogical_bridge, generate_metaphor) get higher future routing bias. Sheogorath stays an imagination program; XM-1 stays the ammunition magazine. The separation is: XM-1 = vocabulary, Sheogorath = engine, CHEESE = reinforcement signal, folds = operating boundaries.",
    "The ammunition cycle: XM-1 stores operator patterns with weights. Sheogorath selects and fires operators to generate candidates. Constraints (domain, contradiction, coherence) filter candidates. Accepted candidates earn CHEESE. CHEESE modifies operator weights for future routing. Rejected candidates leave only trace records. This is reinforcement learning without a neural network."
  ],
